    "body": "I read your issue about hour ago, said to my self 'meh', and started searches.\r\nIn general, you can compile it yourself, it's not that hard. \r\n\r\nIn common it is described here https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/315#issuecomment-530230019 \r\n\r\n1. Install `rust`, `cargo`, \r\n1. Install `cross` (`cargo install cross`)and container service (I used docker)\r\n1. Checkout `starship` git repo, navigate to the directory \r\n1. Edit  `Cargo.toml`:\r\n    ```diff\r\n      [dependencies]\r\n    + openssl = { version = \"0.10.29\", features = [\"vendored\"] }\r\n      # the rest of dependencies...\r\n    ```\r\n    I have no idea why that is needed, I don't really know Rust. Also, I'm not sure about openssl version. =)\r\n    Otherwise you will get an error at build time:\r\n\r\n   ```sh\r\n   --- stderr\r\n   thread 'main' panicked at '\r\n   \r\n   Could not find directory of OpenSSL installation, and this `-sys` crate cannot\r\n   proceed without this knowledge. If OpenSSL is installed and this crate had\r\n   trouble finding it,  you can set the `OPENSSL_DIR` environment variable for the\r\n   compilation process.\r\n   ```\r\n   ... and so on.\r\n\r\n1. Run command:\r\n      `cross build --release --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` \r\n    Choose the target you need from [this list here](https://github.com/rust-embedded/cross#supported-targets)\r\n\r\n1. Copy that baby `./target/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/release/starship` to your device.\r\n\r\n1. ????\r\n\r\n1. PROFIT\r\n    ```bash\r\n    ubuntu on ubuntu in ~\r\n    ❯ uname -a\r\n    Linux ubuntu 5.4.0-1012-raspi #12-Ubuntu SMP Wed May 27 04:08:35 UTC 2020 aarch64 aarch64 aarch64 GNU/Linux\r\n    ```",
