    "updated_at": "2020-07-30T14:40:00Z",
    "body": "> Since it looks like the binaries are created by GitHub Actions, I think it could pretty much be as simple as adding\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n>         include:\r\n>           - target: arm-unknown-linux-gnueabihf\r\n>             os: ubuntu-latest\r\n>             name: starship-arm-unknown-linux-gnueabihf.tar.gz\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> to the [deploy.yml](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/.github/workflows/deploy.yml)\r\n> \r\n> Here's an example workflow that works: https://github.com/phiresky/ripgrep-all/blob/master/.github/workflows/release.yml\r\n\r\nstarship depends on openssl on linux with glibc (libgit might need work too) so unless we vendor it like in the MUSL builds or disable the http client, cargo needs to be directed to an aarch64 openssl directory on cross builds. musl builds, windows and macos builds might work already because they don't use openssl or vendor it.\r\nIf this work isn't done, at some point I expect github actions to add native aarch64 build servers because the architecture is gaining popularity.\r\n",
